# kea FHS migration: runtime /run/kea* -> /var/run/kea/.
#
# Archaeology: -Drunstatedir was the relative "run", which meson
# prefix-joins to /usr/run/kea (PIDFILE_DIR, payload empty dir),
# while the initds tracked flat /run/kea-*.pid files that no build
# ever wrote - a three-way disagreement. Absolute /var/run makes
# pidfiles (/var/run/kea/<daemon>.pid), control sockets and the
# payload dir agree, and the initds track the real pidfiles.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - PID files: cleared at (re)start in both inits (tracked-start
#   only, never against a live daemon); daemons rewrite them and
#   delete their own on clean exit.
# - Control sockets: daemon-managed inside the rundir.
# - New /var/run/kea: converged here on upgrade (root-owned 0755;
#   the suite runs as root, no accounts.d identity); created by
#   checkpath (OpenRC), ExecStartPre (systemd), and the payload.
# - Old /run/kea: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty;
#   left in place and reported while old daemons run. Old flat
#   /run/kea-*.pid files were never written by any build - tmpfs
#   orphans needing no migration.

dir /var/run/kea 0755 root root
rmdir-if-empty /run/kea
